    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0057" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.24/2239: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-16T00:00:00-04:00">June 16,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4783. Please wire fullest information available and recent developments on the
                    contracts referred to in your 4426 and 4427, June 2.<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d36-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please point out to appropriate Foreign Office officials that such long-term
                    contracts on a strictly bilateral basis, extending perhaps <pb facs="0058"
                        n="48" xml:id="pg48"/> well into the post-hostilities period, would have to
                    be viewed by this Government in the light of Article VIII of the United
                    States–United Kingdom trade agreement<anchor n="63" xml:id="d36-f2"/> and might
                    be in conflict with the provisions with regard to state trading as contemplated
                    in the United States–British exploratory commercial-policy talks of last autumn
                    and the resulting joint statement. Please wire also result of your
                    interview.</p>
                <p>Ottawa is being requested<anchor n="64" xml:id="d36-f3"/> to talk with External
                    Affairs along similar lines. Canberra, Wellington and Pretoria are being
                    informed by telegraph.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d36-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d36-f1" n="62" xml:id="d36-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; they contained reports regarding British negotiations for the
                    conclusion of long-term contracts with overseas countries for meat and dairy
                    products (841.24/2237, 2239).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f2" n="63" xml:id="d36-f2-content">
                <p>Signed November 17, 1938: for text, see Department of State Executive Agreement
                    Series No. 164, or 54 Stat. (pt. 2) 1897.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f3" n="64" xml:id="d36-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 44, June 16, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f4" n="65" xml:id="d36-f4-content">
                <p>Telegrams 74, 217, and 80, respectively, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
